From 53e02bf8daf886d07ad67a55f09733d805e69dfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 5yndr0m <sdilanjana21@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 09:06:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build events UI: homepage month grid, month listing, event
 booking page

Wires the Sanity-backed events/monthly-banner data layer into real
pages, matching the client's spec:

Homepage (src/app/page.tsx):
- The events section was a static hardcoded 3-card carousel (and had
  regressed back to the old /payment-with-no-booking-id bug on one
  card after the Frontend branch merge). Replaced with a real
  3-column grid fetched from getUpcomingMonthlyBanners(3): banner
  poster on top, month name/tagline/departure count/"See More" link
  below each -- the "3 flyers in one row, details below each, 2 rows
  3 columns" layout from the brief. Empty state included for before
  any monthlyEventBanner docs exist in Studio.

/events/[month] (new):
- The "See More" destination. Hero banner (reusing the site's
  existing .page-hero pattern from About/Blog/etc for visual
  consistency) followed by a grid of that month's event flyers, each
  showing the flyer image, date, price, includes icons, short
  description, a "Know about the experience" link to the matching
  /experiences/[slug] page (reviews/gallery live there, not here --
  per the brief), and a "Reserve Spot" button. Handles a valid month
  with zero events (empty state) separately from a malformed slug
  (404).

/events/[month]/[eventSlug] (new):
- The booking destination. Mirrors the existing /experiences/[slug]
  detail page's layout (hero image, sticky price/booking panel) but
  for a specific scheduled departure: fixed date instead of a picker,
  spots-remaining shown when the event has a maxParticipants cap, and
  registration-closed/fully-booked states that hide the form instead
  of letting someone book into a full or closed departure.
- New EventBookingForm.tsx: same shape as the existing BookingForm.tsx
  (explicit light-theme styling, not dependent on globals.css's
  .booking-form-scoped dark rules) but posts eventId instead of
  experienceId, and has no date field since the event fixes it.

Also fixed two more instances of the "Book Now" button linking
straight to /payment with no booking_id (Header's nav-cta + mobile
menu, Footer's sticky mobile CTA) -- now point at the events section/
page, which is the actual primary booking entry point per the brief.
Updated payment page's no-booking-id empty state copy/links to match.

Added an "Events" link to the header nav (desktop + mobile) so the
new pages are reachable outside of the homepage grid.

Not touched: ActivitiesCarousel.tsx and the old
MonthlyEventFlyers.tsx/monthlyEvents.ts static data files no longer
exist in the repo (removed by the Frontend branch merge before this
work started) -- nothing to reconcile there.

Verified: tsc --noEmit clean across the whole project. eslint clean
on every new/touched file except two "any" types in
events/[month]/page.tsx for loosely-typed Sanity image fields,
matching the same convention already used throughout this codebase
(e.g. heroImage?: any elsewhere). next build compiles all routes;
only failure is the sandbox's Google Fonts network block, same as
every previous build attempt in this environment, unrelated to this
change.
